/www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-map-pin h-3 w-3 text-muted-foreground" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 10c0 4.993-5.539 10.193-7.399 11.799a1 1 0 0 1-1.202 0C9.539 20.193 4 14.993 4 10a8 8 0 0 1 16 0" /><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3" /></svg>India</li><li class="flex items-center gap-1.5"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-map-pin h-3 w-3 text-muted-foreground" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 10c0 4.993-5.539 10.193-7.399 11.799a1 1 0 0 1-1.202 0C9.539 20.193 4 14.993 4 10a8 8 0 0 1 16 0" /><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3" /></svg>China</li></ul></div></div></div><div class="mt-16 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="font-display text-3xl mb-6">Export FAQ</h2><div class="space-y-3"><details class="group p-5 rounded-xl bg-card border border-border"><summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium list-none flex items-center justify-between gap-4">Which Egyptian port does my granite ship from?<span class="text-gold group-open:rotate-45 transition shrink-0">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">Most shipments depart from Alexandria, Port Said, or Sokhna. The loading port is named in your quotation.</p></details><details class="group p-5 rounded-xl bg-card border border-border"><summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium list-none flex items-center justify-between gap-4">Can I mix multiple Egyptian granites in one container?<span class="text-gold group-open:rotate-45 transition shrink-0">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">Yes. Mixed containers across granite types, finishes, and thicknesses are welcome — this is one of the most efficient ways to source for a multi-product project.</p></details><details class="group p-5 rounded-xl bg-card border border-border"><summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium list-none flex items-center justify-between gap-4">What is FOB vs CIF?<span class="text-gold group-open:rotate-45 transition shrink-0">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">FOB (Free On Board) quotes material loaded onto the vessel at the Egyptian port; you arrange ocean freight and insurance. CIF (Cost, Insurance, Freight) quotes material delivered to your destination port with freight and insurance included.</p></details><details class="group p-5 rounded-xl bg-card border border-border"><summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium list-none flex items-center justify-between gap-4">Do you arrange third-party inspection?<span class="text-gold group-open:rotate-45 transition shrink-0">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">Yes — SGS, Bureau Veritas, and Intertek inspections can be arranged on request before container sealing.</p></details><details class="group p-5 rounded-xl bg-card border border-border"><summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium list-none flex items-center justify-between gap-4">What documents are issued per shipment?<span class="text-gold group-open:rotate-45 transition shrink-0">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">Commercial invoice, packing list, certificate of origin, bill of lading, ISPM-15 fumigation certificate, and inspection certificates as required.</p></details></div></div><div class="mt-14"><a href="<?php echo esc_url(home_url('/contact')); ?>" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium transition bg-foreground text-background hover:opacity-90 shadow-sm">Request Export Quotation</a></div></section><!--/$--></main>
